    A compiled object with no asString prints its bare Fortress type name

    trait Object's compiled default becomes jDefaultAsString(self), one native
    in stringOps that keeps a value's own Java toString when its class declares
    one and otherwise renders the stamped class name in walk's spelling (Box,
    Cell[\ZZ32\], Pt, (A,B), A->B), as Pavol decided for row 321; before it the
    default recursed through FValue.toString until the stack overflowed.
    DefaultRenderRungS gates it with 18 assertions. One case of row 321 stays
    open and is gated as an expected failure by XXXFortToStringRungS, placed at
    the gather: an object with a zero-argument Fortress member named toString
    still overflows. Rows 363-369 opened, notes appended to rows 76, 307 and
    321; R's prelude citations this rung's import line moved are re-anchored,
    and row 362 is measured unaffected by the new default.

